  "about": "Run outcomes for one mutable or append-only stream after a base of three records (a, b, z). decision is what each side does to the stream's other-device copy: replace (drop what the run omits) or merge (same-key merge only). Intake sees: outcome, collection, timeRange, semantics, records, skippedDelete, oversize, covered. The desktop producer sees: mode, detailGap, proof, records, semantics. A detail gap reaches intake as covered=false. The completion proof, and a record too large for the writer, reach only one side. producerOnly marks a case where the two sides cannot see the same input. safe=false marks a case where intake replaces and the producer merges.",
